                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              might still be difficult, but we've reduced it to internalising
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cart+Sp"} Cart Sp
              in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/space"} space
              for granted, so you'd have to internalise that into
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              too, but I'm not sure how important that really is, when I think about how the topology on a smooth manifold can be recovered from the smooth structure.)
            %p
              %em> Rafael
              \: Can someone that knows more than me about this add the result of this question to this article so nobody have to ask again.
            %p
              %em> Toby
              \: I'd rather not, since it's all ‘I think’ and ‘might be difficult’; it's better as a query box, moved to the bottom if necessary. But if Todd agrees with me, then maybe he'll add it.
          %h3#definition_via_cartologies Definition via cartologies
          .query
            %p
              Note: the following is tentative “original research”. It is prompted by the desire to extend the pseudogroup approach for defining general notions of manifold, so as to cover also an appropriate general notion of “map”. Comments, improvements, and corrections are encouraged –
              = succeed "." do
                %em Todd
            %p I've read through it once, and it makes sense. I'll read through it again more carefully later. —Toby
          %p
            We begin by defining the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-poset"} 2-poset
            (i.e., locally
            = succeed "ed" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/preorder"} preorder
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bicategory"} bicategory
            = succeed "," do
              %strong regions
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Reg
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Reg
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/partial+functions"} partial functions
            with open domain, that is spans
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mover
                    %mo ←
                    %mi i
                  %mi U
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mi f
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \overset{i}{\leftarrow} U \overset{f}{\to} Y
          %p
            where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            is continuous and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi i
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i
            is an open embedding. The spans are locally (that is, for fixed
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            and
            = succeed ")" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
          %p
            These local posets are not cocomplete, but they admit certain obvious
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/joins"} joins
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi U
                    %mi α
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi f
                    %mi α
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo :
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (U_\alpha, f_\alpha): X \to Y
          %p
            the join
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ⋁
                    %mi α
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi U
                    %mi α
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi f
                    %mi α
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \bigvee_\alpha (U_\alpha, f_\alpha)
            exists iff we have local compatibility:
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi f
                    %mi α
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi U
                        %mi α
                      %mo ∩
                      %msub
                        %mi U
                        %mi β
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mi f
                    %mi β
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi U
                        %mi α
                      %mo ∩
                      %msub
                        %mi U
                        %mi β
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_{\alpha}|_{U_\alpha \cap U_\beta} = f_{\beta}|_{U_\alpha \cap U_\beta}
          %p
            for all
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
