            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supermanifold"} supermanifold
              %ul
                %li
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Euclidean+supermanifold"} Euclidean supermanifold
                  (notice that the definition of that is very much along the lines of the Klein-program-style definition above).
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/semialgebraic+manifold"} semialgebraic manifold
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dimension+of+a+manifold"} dimension of a manifold
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/low-dimensional+topology"} low-dimensional topology
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/projective+manifold"} projective manifold
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/manifold+with+boundary"} manifold with boundary
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closed+manifold"} closed manifold
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/product+manifold"} product manifold
          %h2#references References
          %blockquote
            %p
              For more see the references at
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differentiable+manifold"} differentiable manifold
              and
              = succeed "." do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifold"} smooth manifold
          %p The vision of the modern notion of manifolds is attributed to:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bernhard+Riemann"}> Bernhard Riemann
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%C3%9Cber+die+Hypothesen%2C+welche+der+Geometrie+zu+Grunde+liegen"} Über die Hypothesen, welche der Geometrie zu Grunde liegen
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-642-35121-1"} doi:10.1007/978-3-642-35121-1
              %p
                Engl. transl:
                = succeed ":" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/William+Clifford"} William Clifford
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/On+the+hypotheses+which+underlie+geometry"} On the hypotheses which underlie geometry
                %strong VIII
                (1873) 183-184 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-319-26042-6"}> doi:10.1007/978-3-319-26042-6
                \&amp;rbrack;
          %p See also:
          %ul
            %li
              John Loftin,
              %em The real definition of a smooth manifold
              (
              %a{:href => "http://andromeda.rutgers.edu/~loftin/difffal03/manifold.pdf"}> pdf
